---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const b = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const faqs = [
  ['How much does Booke AI cost compared with Financial Cents Month-End Close?', 'Booke AI Business is $129 per business per month; the firm plan is custom-priced. Financial Cents Month-End Close is a $5 per client per month add-on, billed annually, on top of a Financial Cents plan: Solo $19/mo, Team $49/user/mo or Scale $69/user/mo (annual), all on a 12-month agreement.'],
  ['Do Booke AI and Financial Cents MEC do the same job?', 'No. Booke AI works every day, categorizing the bank feed with AI and matching documents. Financial Cents MEC works at close: transaction review, uncategorized transactions, reconciliation and the client chase, inside a practice management plan.'],
  ['What do they cost for 20 clients?', 'At list price, Booke AI Business is 20 × $129 = $2,580 per month. Financial Cents MEC is $119 per month for a solo firm (Solo $19 plus $100 MEC) or $247 for a 3-person firm on Team. A solo firm running both pays $2,699 per month before any Booke firm discount.'],
  ['Which ledgers do they support?', 'Booke AI works with QuickBooks Online and Xero. Financial Cents MEC syncs corrections back to QuickBooks Online only.'],
];
const faqLd = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a } })),
});
---
<Base
  title="Booke AI vs Financial Cents Month-End Close — AI categorization vs close review"
  description="Booke AI ($129/business/mo, daily AI categorization and document matching in QBO and Xero) vs the Financial Cents Month-End Close add-on ($5/client/mo on a Financial Cents plan, QBO review, uncategorized transactions and reconciliation): what each automates and 20-client cost math. Prices verified Oct 2026."
>
  <h1>Booke AI vs Financial Cents Month-End Close</h1>
  <p>These sit at different points of the month. Booke AI works every day: it categorizes the bank feed with AI, matches documents, and hands your staff the exceptions. Financial Cents Month-End Close (MEC) works at close: it is a $5/client add-on to the Financial Cents practice management plans where you review client books, chase uncategorized transactions, reconcile accounts and sync corrections back to QuickBooks Online. Booke reduces the coding work; MEC organizes the review and the client chase that is left.</p>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th></th><th><a href={`${b}/tools/booke-ai`}>Booke AI</a></th><th><a href={`${b}/tools/financial-cents`}>Financial Cents MEC</a></th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Best for</td><td>Firms whose hours go into coding bank transactions every day</td><td>Firms on (or moving to) Financial Cents that want the close review and client chase inside their workflows</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Pricing (verified Oct 2026)</td><td>AI Bookkeeper (Business): $129 per business/month, prorated when you add a business mid-period. Firm plan (multi-client management, white-label, priority onboarding) is custom-priced.</td><td>MEC add-on $5/client/month, billed annually, on top of a plan: Solo $19/mo, Team $49/user/mo, Scale $69/user/mo (annual; Team $69 and Scale $89 monthly with a 5-user minimum). All plans are a 12-month agreement.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Ledger</td><td>QuickBooks Online and Xero</td><td>QuickBooks Online (corrections sync back to QBO)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>What it automates</td><td>Daily bank feed categorization, smart document matching, missing document requests, custom thresholds and rules, OCR for bills, invoices and receipts, exception review with audit trail</td><td>Transaction review, uncategorized transactions, account reconciliation, 1099 and W-9 prep, shared transactions, newly added vendors and accounts</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Also gives you</td><td>Nothing outside bookkeeping; it is not practice management</td><td>Practice management: workflows, client portal, client tasks and requests (auto follow-ups on Scale), time tracking, billing</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Cost at 20 clients (list prices, monthly)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Booke AI Business: 20 × $129 = $2,580. The firm plan is custom-priced, so a firm this size would likely ask for a quote.</li>
    <li>Financial Cents MEC, solo firm: Solo $19 plus MEC 20 × $5 = $100, so $119.</li>
    <li>Financial Cents MEC, 3-person firm: Team 3 × $49 = $147 plus MEC $100, so $247.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The numbers are not like for like. Booke replaces daily coding labor; MEC is the review and chase step plus a practice management plan. A solo firm running both pays $2,699 a month at list, before any Booke firm discount. Financial Cents is billed annually on a 12-month agreement. All figures before discounts or promotions.</p>

  <h2>When to choose Booke AI</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Coding the bank feed is your biggest time cost, not the client chase.</li>
    <li>You have Xero clients; MEC syncs with QuickBooks Online only.</li>
    <li>You want OCR and document matching in the same tool, or a white-labeled client experience (firm plan).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to choose Financial Cents MEC</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You already run the firm on Financial Cents, so close review costs $5/client and sits next to your checklists.</li>
    <li>Your clients are on QuickBooks Online and the bottleneck is review, reconciliation and getting answers from clients.</li>
    <li>You want 1099 and W-9 prep in the same place as month-end review.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  {faqs.map(([q, a]) => (<><h3>{q}</h3><p>{a}</p></>))}
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqLd} />

  <p>Sources: booke.ai/pricing and financial-cents.com/pricing, checked 2026-10-19. No sponsor has paid for this comparison.</p>

  <p>
    <a href={`${b}/compare/booke-ai-alternatives`}>Booke AI alternatives</a> ·
    <a href={`${b}/compare/financial-cents-alternatives`}>Financial Cents alternatives</a> ·
    <a href={`${b}/compare/booke-ai-vs-uncat`}>Booke AI vs Uncat</a> ·
    <a href={`${b}/compare/uncat-vs-financial-cents`}>Uncat vs Financial Cents MEC</a> ·
    <a href={`${b}/compare/xenett-vs-financial-cents`}>Xenett vs Financial Cents MEC</a>
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1rem 0; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: #f6f6f6; }
</style>
